# Public repository docs policy (decided 2026-07-12): of the numbered docs/ folders, only
# docs/02-architecture/ and docs/03-development/ are intentionally public. Every other
# numbered docs/ folder is internal planning/governance material and must never reach the
# public repository - ignored at the folder level (not per-file) so a new file added to any
# of these later is covered automatically rather than requiring someone to remember to add it.
docs/00-overview/
docs/01-product/
docs/04-research/
docs/05-business/
docs/06-operations/
docs/07-governance/

# Finance Bill 2024 report deliverables placed directly in docs/ root (2026-07-12) -
# not covered by the folder-level rules above since they sit at docs/ top level, not
# inside a numbered subfolder. Not public-facing: a draft under active revision.
docs/CLIO_Finance_Bill_2024_Case_Study_Public.pdf
docs/CLIO_Finance_Bill_2024_Incident_Report_final.pdf

# Session-local relay reports (2026-08-01) - disposable scratch written at the repo
# root by a live-repo Claude Code session, meant to be pasted back into the separate
# planning environment by hand. Never staged or committed, including by the project
# owner's own later action.
reports.md

# TD-132 pre-commit content-check denylist companion (2026-09-02) - holds the actual
# real sensitive strings (names, quoted private reasoning) this project has had to
# redact once already. Must never be tracked: committing it would leak exactly the
# content check_public_docs.py exists to keep out of CLAUDE.md/decision-log.md. The
# tracked sensitive_terms.yml next to it holds only generic categories/patterns and
# is safe to publish.
Bruin/scripts/content_check/sensitive_terms.local.yml

# ADR-0010 llm_report_writer/ live comparison run output (2026-08-03) - per-run
# generated JSON, not source, disposable/regeneratable via run_live_windows.py.
llm_report_writer/run_live_windows_results.json

# TD-100/ADR-0013 agreement-check harness: per-run fetch checkpoints (which
# report_ids a specific run has already pulled from OONI's API). Disposable
# resume state, not source -- distinct from config/coverage_log.json (the
# cross-run rotation log), which IS versioned.
Bruin/scripts/agreement_check/.checkpoints/

